cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite the bayescompR package in publications use:'
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-only
title: 'bayescompR: Pure R Implementation of the Stan Modeling Language'
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-11-15'
abstract: >-
  A pure R implementation of the Stan modeling language (version 2.40) and
  of many inference algorithms. Stan programs are parsed, type checked and
  compiled into R closures on a reverse mode automatic differentiation tape,
  and fitted with the No-U-Turn sampler and the other CmdStan methods, with
  CmdStan's adaptation, output files and diagnostics, as well as many
  further samplers and approximations. No C++ compiler, CmdStan or rstan is
  required. Not affiliated with or endorsed by the Stan Development Team or
  NumFOCUS.
authors:
  - family-names: Sophie
    given-names: Adam R
    email: adamrsophie@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/adamrsophie/bayescompR
url: https://adamrsophie.github.io/bayescompR/
keywords:
  - bayesian-inference
  - stan
  - probabilistic-programming
  - mcmc
  - hamiltonian-monte-carlo
  - automatic-differentiation
  - variational-inference
  - r
